# Team Module (MVP)

MVP has exactly one team: **Ranches Thunders**.

Do not build multi-team switching UX. Schema may keep `team_id` for future tenancy, but product behavior is single-team.

## Lifecycle

- Seeded at migrate time; Admin may update settings (logo, WhatsApp notify config, UPI id)
- Never hard-delete the team
- Archive only if product later needs it (not MVP UI)

## Membership

- Admin adds players; until then, login may succeed but app access is denied
- A user belongs to Ranches Thunders via `team_memberships`
- Roles on membership: `admin` | `player`
- Admins are players too (`role = admin` still participates in polls/payments)
- Store role/status/joined_at on membership — never on the global user alone

## Ownership

- At least one Admin must remain
- Transfer admin before demoting/removing the last Admin

## Settings (team-owned)

- Display name / logo
- WhatsApp group notify hook (existing group)
- UPI payment destination for settlements
- Default match fee / carpool fee constants (carpool = ₹100 to-and-fro)

## Validation

- No duplicate active memberships for the same user
- Inactive / non-member → access denied
- Do not allow creating additional teams in MVP services
